Bug: The WHERE clause in the UPDATE uses '==' which is not valid SQL. Use a single equals sign '='. Corrected snippet:
```CREATE TABLE employees (id INT, name VARCHAR(50), salary INT);
INSERT INTO employees (id, name, salary) VALUES (1, 'Alice', 70000);
INSERT INTO employees (id, name, salary) VALUES (3, 'Bob', 60000);
UPDATE employees SET salary = salary + 5000 WHERE id = 3;
SELECT * FROM employees WHERE id = 3;```
